# SynapseGate: one-click API requests for VS Code.
#
# 1. Install the "REST Client" extension (VS Code will suggest it when you open this folder).
# 2. Start the server:  npm start
# 3. Click "Send Request" above any request below. Run them from the top, in order:
#    later requests use the ticket id returned by the first one.
#
# Demo keys (change them with the VIEWER_KEY / AGENT_KEY / ADMIN_KEY environment variables).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/v1
@viewerKey = viewer-key-123
@agentKey = agent-key-123
@adminKey = admin-key-123

### ---------------------------------------------------------- Public (no key needed)

### API index
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### Health (the system pulse)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Documentation generated from the code, with runnable curl examples
GET {{baseUrl}}/docs

### ---------------------------------------------------------- Tickets

### 1. Create a ticket (agent). Expect 201, score 90, critical
# @name createTicket
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets
x-api-key: {{agentKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{
  "email": "asha@example.com",
  "title": "Checkout page is down #{{$randomInt 100 999}}",
  "description": "Customers cannot pay, urgent fix needed.",
  "category": "outage",
  "affectedUsers": 150
}

### 2. List tickets (viewer). Try the filters: priority, status, category, assignee, search, overdue, createdFrom, createdTo
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets?priority=critical&sort=-score&page=1&limit=10
x-api-key: {{viewerKey}}

### 3. Search
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets?search=checkout
x-api-key: {{viewerKey}}

### 4. One ticket
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{createTicket.response.body.$.data.id}}
x-api-key: {{viewerKey}}

### 5. Assign it
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{createTicket.response.body.$.data.id}}/assignee
x-api-key: {{agentKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "assignee": "Ravi Kumar" }

### 6. Move it forward: in_progress, then resolved (going back returns 400)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{createTicket.response.body.$.data.id}}/status
x-api-key: {{agentKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "in_progress" }

### 7. Add a comment
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{createTicket.response.body.$.data.id}}/comments
x-api-key: {{agentKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "Payment provider confirmed an outage on their side." }

### 8. List comments
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{createTicket.response.body.$.data.id}}/comments
x-api-key: {{viewerKey}}

### 9. History (audit trail)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{createTicket.response.body.$.data.id}}/history
x-api-key: {{viewerKey}}

### 10. Override the priority (admin only, reason required)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{createTicket.response.body.$.data.id}}/priority
x-api-key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "priority": "high", "reason": "Impact is smaller than first reported" }

### 11. Statistics
GET {{baseUrl}}/stats
x-api-key: {{viewerKey}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------- Admin

### Metrics: latency, availability, errors (admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/metrics
x-api-key: {{adminKey}}

### Recent API requests (admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/logs?limit=20
x-api-key: {{adminKey}}

### Notifier status (admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/notifier
x-api-key: {{adminKey}}

### Failure simulator: make the notifier fail (then create 4 critical tickets and watch the circuit open)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/admin/notifier
x-api-key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mode": "failing" }

### Failure simulator: make it healthy again
PUT {{baseUrl}}/admin/notifier
x-api-key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mode": "healthy" }

### Delete the ticket (admin only; an agent key returns 403)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{createTicket.response.body.$.data.id}}
x-api-key: {{adminKey}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------- Errors on purpose

### 401: no API key
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets

### 400: the Gatekeeper rejects a bad ticket and explains every problem
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets
x-api-key: {{agentKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "ab", "category": "nonsense", "extra": true }

### 403: a viewer cannot create tickets
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets
x-api-key: {{viewerKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "a@b.co", "title": "Viewer tries to write", "description": "This must be refused.", "category": "bug" }

### 404: unknown ticket
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets/tkt_9999
x-api-key: {{viewerKey}}
